# Python environment (729MB, regenerable via requirements.txt)
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Model weight symlinks (host-specific paths into local Ollama blob storage,
# invalid on any other machine anyway)
gguf/

# HF publish staging directories: this IS the content already published to
# huggingface.co/DarkStarDeleeuw, kept out of git per the "data lives on HF,
# this repo holds code/docs" split. See MANIFEST.md for the live dataset URLs.
hf_upload/
hf_upload2/
hf_upload_*/

# Recruiter-trial raw source data: already folded into the published HF
# dataset (DarkStarDeleeuw/bluedot-unit2-recruiter-pilot-gemma3-12b).
recruiter-trial/results/*/

# Large raw run logs (multi-MB): too big for the "small evidence" convention
# other run_*.log files follow, and every one below is either regenerable or
# already folded into a published HF dataset.
run_free_screens.log
run_nla-screen-qwen25-7b.log

# Raw eval logs and activation tensors: regenerable from the harness, or
# already folded into a published HF dataset. Local-only copies stay on disk,
# not in git. See MANIFEST.md "Local-only, not in git or on HF" section for
# anything here that hasn't been published anywhere yet.
logs/
llamacpp_logs/
*.eval
**/acts/*.bin
*.bin

# Nested clone of the upstream ImpossibleBench project (has its own git
# history, not ours to absorb) — see README for the clone instructions.
repo/

# Kaggle kernel run outputs (large, regenerable)
moe-floor/kernels/*/output/

# MoE-floor Kaggle results: keep small summaries/sidecars, exclude raw transcripts+tokens+logs (policy: transcripts/activations -> HF or local-only)
moe-floor/results/*/transcripts.jsonl
moe-floor/results/*/tokens/
moe-floor/results/*/*.log

# Oversized run logs (added 2026-09-07). Both were swept into git by a `git add -A`
# and would have blocked or bloated the push:
#   olmo3/cpu_load_test.log        1.9 GB, left by an earlier session; GitHub's hard
#                                  limit is 100 MB, so this alone made the push fail.
#   run_northmini_realbatch.log    ~30 MB and still growing; it was committed 10 times
#                                  as it grew, ~257 MB of near-duplicate blobs.
# MANIFEST's rule is "small raw run logs -> git". These are not small. Keep them
# local-only like the eval transcripts and activation tensors.
olmo3/cpu_load_test.log   # deleted 2026-09-07; see cpu_load_test_SALVAGED.md
run_northmini_realbatch.log

# north-mini big batch (2026-09-08): screen-only dir with NO activations, fully published
# at DarkStarDeleeuw/bluedot-unit2-concealment-probe-north-mini-code under bigbatch/.
# Its samples.jsonl (21 MB) and rendered teacher-forcing tokens (76 MB) stay out of git per
# the "data lives on HF, this repo holds code/docs" split; the small sidecars that the
# findings ledger cites (mechanism_audit.json, manifests, prioritize.log, skipped_sids.json)
# ARE tracked.
concealment-probe/data/north-mini-bigbatch/*/tokens/
concealment-probe/data/north-mini-bigbatch/*/samples.jsonl

# SAE causal/harvest run outputs: generated continuations (large, and each run is
# tied to one server config). Rows + control vectors go to HF with the run.
sae-causal/*.jsonl
sae-causal/*.log
sae-causal/*.pid
bystander/acts_*.predecision/

# Activation capture trees and HF staging (2026-09-13). *.bin was already ignored, but the
# sidecars were not: 3,859 files / 41.7 MB of token streams, manifests and extract logs sat
# one `git add -A` away from the repo. These trees ARE the published HF content -- one home,
# not two (storage policy in CLAUDE.md) -- and the 2026-09-07 incident that put a 1.9 GB log
# into fifteen unpushed commits is why staging is deliberate here.
bystander/acts_*/
bystander/.hf_stage/
bystander/.*_env/
visualizations/out2/
.envcache_gpu*/

# sae-causal token streams (2026-09-22): 140 MB of rendered token streams from the steering arm.
# Same policy as the other tokens/ entries above -- transcripts, tokens and activations go to
# Hugging Face or stay local-only, never into git.
sae-causal/tokens/
sae-causal/tokens_negatives/
sae-causal/tokens_positives/
